    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0929" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg869"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 89.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1868-08-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 22, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have your dispatch of the 22d of July,
                    No. 131. It affords me much pleasure to know that the secretary for foreign
                    affairs in Chili <pb facs="0930" n="870" xml:id="pg870"/> expressed himself to
                    you as being entirely willing to accept the first proposition of the United
                    States for an indefinite truce in the war between the allied republics and
                    Spain. I take notice further that the Chilian secretary said to you that he had
                    no objections to adjust the matter by means of a congress of plenipotentiaries;
                    as proposed by the United States, but that as a party measure it might
                    materially injure the present administration in Chili.</p>
                <p>Insomuch as this information comes in an indirect as well as informal manner, I
                    am obliged to limit myself in the use of it to a simple mention of the matter
                    thus noticed to the Spanish minister plenipotentiary here for the information of
                    his government.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvin P. Hovey</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
